    `(2)(c) the Commissioner specifies that date in the notice under Article 16(1) or (2)`  IS FALSE
    `(2)(d) the Commissioner determines that the deregistration should take effect retrospectively`  IS FALSE
    `there remains any property of the charity that was acquired before it was deregistered (the 'remaining property')`  IS TRUE
    `the entity continues to apply the remaining property for the preserved charitable purposes`  IS FALSE
    `the entity continues to apply the remaining property in accordance with the preserved public benefit statement`  IS FALSE
    `a provision of the entity's constitution or constitutional Law purports to empower the entity to amend the preserved charitable purposes or preserved public benefit statement`  IS FALSE
    `the application under paragraph (9) is made by the Attorney General`  IS FALSE
    `the application under paragraph (9) is made by a governor of the entity`  IS TRUE
    `(9)(a) it appears to the court that there is or has been any conduct in the administration of the entity in relation to the remaining property, that would have been misconduct if the entity had not been deregistered`  IS TRUE
    `(9)(b) it appears to the court that it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power for the purpose of protecting the remaining property or securing a proper application of the remaining property for the preserved charitable purposes of the entity and in accordance with the preserved public benefit statement`  IS TRUE
    `the governor has first given notice to the Attorney General of the governor's intention to apply under paragraph (9) and of the reasons for that intention`  IS FALSE   -- the failure

#ASSERT NOT `Article 17(10) — a governor's application is competent` `a governor's application, without notice to the Attorney General`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 17(9) — the court's power over the deregistered entity arises` `a governor's application, without notice to the Attorney General`
-- 17(6) is BREACHED on these facts too: the remaining property is not being applied for the
-- preserved charitable purposes. That is precisely what the governor wants the court to fix.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 17(6) — the entity applies the remaining property for the preserved purposes` `a governor's application, without notice to the Attorney General`

-- The SAME governor, who this time gives the Attorney General notice first. The application
